title: Bullous Pemphigoid
---

# Bullous Pemphigoid

- **Definition** - most common immunobullous disease worldwide causing tense bulla and is an autoimmune disease of the elderly
- **Epidemiology:**
  - <u>Prevalence</u> - most common immunobullous disease
  - <u>Demographic</u>:
    - Age - disease of the elderly (average age of onset \> 65y)
    - Sex - M=F
    - Comorbidities - a/w neurological disorders (e.g. stroke, PD, dementia)
- **Pathophysiology of BP:**
  - <u>AutoAb production</u> - detectable autoAb (e.g. BP-230, BP-180) production directed against hemi-desmisomal Ags (e.g. BPAg-1 \[intracellular\], BPAg-2 \[transmembrane type XVII collagen\])
  - <u>Complement activation and inflammation</u> - resulting in local inflammation, hemi-desmosomal damage, loss of cell-cell junction and subsequently subepidermal blistering
- **Clinical features of BP:**
  - <u>Prodromal cutaneous manifestation</u> - lengthy prodromal itchy, urticated, erythematous rash prior to the onset of tense bullae, often w/ milia formation (tense milk spots) due to BM disruption
  - <u>Tense bullae formation</u> - fluid filled vesicles, characterstically over the **trunk, flexures, and limbs** 
  ![](../img/large_tense_bullae_in_bp.png)
  - <u>Mucosal blistering</u> - most commonly over the oral mucosa
- **Ix:**
  - **Skin Bx** - split in two and one sent for direct immunofluoresence and one for FFPE and histology:
    - <u>Histology</u> - subepidermal blistering w/ eosinophilia rich infiltrate
    - <u>Direct IMF</u> - IgG and C3 staining at the basememnt membrane

    
    ![](../img/direct_imf_of_bp.png)
  - **Serology** - indirect IF and ELISA for BP-230 and BP-180:
    - <u>Indirect IF of serum</u> - IgG for w/ +ve titres of circulating anti-epidermal Ab (70%)
    - <u>ELISA</u> - +ve for BP-180 and BP-230
  - **Microbiology** - blister fluids for culture to exclude viral or bacterial infection
- **Mx:**
  - **Principles of Mx:**
    - <u>Escalation of immunosuppressive therapy</u>:
      - Topical potent corticosteroids
      - Systemic corticosteroid
      - Biologics
      - IVIG

    
    ![](../img/evidence_for_tx_of_bp.png)
